"""
THE WORLD IN ONE DAY -- Friday 20 November 2026.
40 stories, 8 regions. Pure-Python front page, stdlib only.

Layout and content copy the manual front page drawn by the user
(Mana) -- masthead + huge serif date + italic subhead + 6-number
strip + 8-tab region bar + 3 lead cards + 5 medium cards + 5 small
cards + world map (droplet pins) + 27-story index + DATE CHECK box
+ footer. All text, numbers and colours are his, reproduced exactly.

Lead: 1 Kyiv bridges, 2 Cyclone Akvan, 3 AI sell-off.
Medium: 4 UK-EU reset, 5 COP31, 6 Poland, 7 Italy, 8 Kenya oil.
Small: 9 Turkiye industry, 10 India GDP, 11 Australia renewables,
12 Brazil dengue, 13 Mexico tourism.
Index 1-27: short headlines only, no sources.
Strip numbers are the ones on Mana's page: 40 / 8 / 300,000+ /
5.1% / GBP 5.1bn / 118 -- reproduced as printed, not re-verified.

Fonts: Liberation (SIL OFL 1.1) outlines embedded below -- no
hand-drawn glyphs, no font files, no network. Output 1024x1024 PNG,
deterministic.
"""

